    ("ltcm-russian-default", "Long-Term Capital Management", 2, "Russian default wiped out the fund", "1998", "Fed-orchestrated $3.6B bailout from 14 banks; LTCM liquidated in 2000.", "LTCM — whose board included Myron Scholes and Robert Merton, both Nobel laureates — used 25:1 leverage on bond-arbitrage trades. The August 1998 Russian default caused a flight to liquidity that unwound LTCM's positions. The New York Fed orchestrated a $3.6B private recapitalisation to avoid systemic risk.", "When Genius Failed — Roger Lowenstein", "Leverage is an option on liquidity; when liquidity disappears, the option is exercised against you."),
